    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d428">

                <pb facs="0584" n="482" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg482"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2403: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-04T17:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 4,
                                1919, 5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5.45
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2969. My 2922, August 29, 5 p.m., regarding Chinese loan consortium.</p>
                <p>I am informally advised by Under Secretary of Foreign Affairs that within an hour
                    after our discussion on August 29, Japanese Ambassador orally informed Foreign
                    Office that his Government greatly desired to participate in consortium with
                    reservations affecting not so much Manchuria and Mongolia as certain districts
                    or portions thereof.</p>
                <pb facs="0585" n="483" xml:id="pg483"/>
                <p>The Ambassador was requested to furnish Foreign Office with a <hi
                        rendition="#italic">précis</hi> of the districts and conditions which has
                    not yet been received and pending the receipt of which Foreign Office can give
                    no definite reply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
